<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. VII — tissue cells as hexagons / froth vs. human corneal endothelium (Pass 1 baseline) (Homo sapiens — corneal endothelium in situ (ocular monolayer epithelium); Elodea canadensis leaf epidermis (secondary))",
        "Thompson (1917) Ch. VII — tissue cells as hexagons / froth vs. human corneal endothelium (Pass 1 baseline) faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens — corneal endothelium in situ (ocular monolayer epithelium); Elodea canadensis leaf epidermis (secondary) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-019-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-019-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-019-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-019-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-019-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-019-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_019.lean, morphoeval/math_kg_loops/thompson1917-t1917-019.yaml implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens — corneal endothelium in situ (ocular monolayer epithelium); Elodea canadensis leaf epidermis (secondary) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_019.lean>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/math_kg_loops/thompson1917-t1917-019.yaml>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens — corneal endothelium in situ (ocular monolayer epithelium); Elodea canadensis leaf epidermis (secondary)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: No scale (um) is attached to the specimen; morphometrics are dimensionless",
        "does_not_claim: No statement about proliferating epithelia beyond the reconstructed division chain",
        "does_not_claim: v1 does not measure any polygon statistic on the corneal endothelium or on Thompson's Fig. 125",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Euler side-sum, mu2, isoperimetric excess perimeter, Lewis and Aboav-Weaire fits on the model (E1-E5)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mean-field Gibson 2006 division-topology Markov chain with through-centre cleavage (E6; reconstruction, not Gibson's exact matrix)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Voronoi froth morphospace with Gaussian positional disorder delta and Lloyd relaxation (not in Thompson)",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson p. 305: cellular tissue resembles a froth",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson p. 309/323: partitions meet three at a point at ~120 degrees (Lamarle minimal-area condition)",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson p. 321: hexagonal pattern illustrated in countless cases but perfectly regular only rarely; eye pigment epithelium as the exemplar",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson p. 325: cells on the average hexagonal, some with fewer and some with more sides than six",
        "reported_in_source: Thompson p. 330: closely packed hexagons give the minimal extent of boundary in a plane",
        "transfer_boundary: Lloyd (centroidal Voronoi) relaxation is a proxy for surface-tension perimeter minimisation; it is not a Plateau/vertex-model energy descent",
        "transfer_boundary: The honeycomb bound is applied cell-by-cell to the measured area distribution (Hales 2001 proves the equal-area case)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-019_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_019.lean, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/math_kg_loops/thompson1917-t1917-019.yaml; output: docs/media/t1917_019_the_forms_of_tissues_or_cell_a_comparison.png; organism: Homo sapiens — corneal endothelium in situ (ocular monolayer epithelium); Elodea canadensis leaf epidermis (secondary); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson p. 305: cellular tissue resembles a froth | Thompson p. 309/323: partitions meet three at a point at ~120 degrees (Lamarle minimal-area condition) | Thompson p. 321: hexagonal pattern illustrated in countless cases but perfectly regular only rarely; eye pigment epithelium as the exemplar | Thompson p. 325: cells on the average hexagonal, some with fewer and some with more sides than six | Thompson p. 330: closely packed hexagons give the minimal extent of boundary in a plane; reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Voronoi froth morphospace with Gaussian positional disorder delta and Lloyd relaxation (not in Thompson) | Euler side-sum, mu2, isoperimetric excess perimeter, Lewis and Aboav-Weaire fits on the model (E1-E5) | Mean-field Gibson 2006 division-topology Markov chain with through-centre cleavage (E6; reconstruction, not Gibson's exact matrix); transfer_boundary: Lloyd (centroidal Voronoi) relaxation is a proxy for surface-tension perimeter minimisation; it is not a Plateau/vertex-model energy descent | The honeycomb bound is applied cell-by-cell to the measured area distribution (Hales 2001 proves the equal-area case); does_not_claim: v1 does not measure any polygon statistic on the corneal endothelium or on Thompson's Fig. 125 | No statement about proliferating epithelia beyond the reconstructed division chain | No scale (um) is attached to the specimen; morphometrics are dimensionless]; other sources: On Growth and Form — Ch. VII The Forms of Tissues, or Cell-Aggregates (pp. 293-345, Figs. 120-127) <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, Morphology of human corneal endothelium in situ (alizarin red) — Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0 <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morphology_of_human_corneal_endothelium_in_situ.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 979 µm (0.0009792 m, log10=-3.009 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (20 runs from 979 µm to 2.85 m): 979 µm:cortical-sulcal-axon-tension, 1.4 mm:bressloff-cowan-V1-hallucination, 1.5 mm:corticothalamic-seizure-spirals, 1.7 mm:homo-sapiens-bioelectric-polarity, 3.1 mm:vertex-glass-jamming, 3.4 mm:homo-sapiens-vertex-packing, 6.3 cm:homo-sapiens-turing-wavelength, 11.7 cm:homo-sapiens-clock-wavefront" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.1090380305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s004540010071>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0026-0800(70)90038-8>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.11.049>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature05014>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/00107518408210979>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1097/ICO.0b013e318033a6da> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-019-overall>,
